{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"},{"kind":"text","text":"<each "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" repeat each "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryTerm","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule9QueryTermP","text":"QueryTerm"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A query has ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"terms","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"filter","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". Each term is either a component type, which an entity must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hold and whose value the query reads, or an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" group, which an entity matches by holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at least one of its types. The filter adds conditions that read nothing: types an entity must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or must not hold, components added or changed since a tick, and relations. An entity matches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the query when it matches every term and passes the filter.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A query doesn’t belong to any world. Build it once, store it, compare it with another, and run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it against any world. The following example finds the entities that move and aren’t frozen:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Name(value: \"comet\"), Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"statue\"), Position(x: 4, y: 2), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0), Frozen())","world.spawn(Name(value: \"moon\"), Position(x: 9, y: 9))","","let movers = Query(Name.self, Position.self, Velocity.self).without(Frozen.self)","","var names: [String] = []","for (_, name, _, _) in world.query(movers) {","    names.append(name.value)","}","print(names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"comet\"]\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each row starts with the entity, labeled "},{"code":"entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", followed by one value per term in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the query lists them. The statue holds every term but is frozen, and the moon has no velocity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To change components while you visit them, pass a query to ","type":"text"},{"code":"update(_:over:body:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"following example moves every entity that has a velocity and isn’t frozen:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let comet = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","let statue = world.spawn(Position(x: 4, y: 2), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0), Frozen())","","world.update(Position.self, over: Query(Velocity.self).without(Frozen.self)) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: comet])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\"","print(world[Position.self, of: statue])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 4.0, y: 2.0)\""]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a parameter of a system, a query arrives bound to the world the system runs on, and you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterate it directly. A system spells its filter as types; see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query\/Where"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Queries of one to three terms, each a component or an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf"},{"type":"text","text":" group of two to four types, run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through code specialized for their exact shape. Other shapes take a general path that does more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work per entity."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/SH","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","title":"Query","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}],"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Query","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:11WorldModule5QueryV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Query.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Query.swift#L56"}},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"m